Are not these herbs sublimely fragrant? They sweeten the air and lend freshness to even the foulest room.	難道這些藥草不是芳香無比嗎？它們能使空氣芬芳，即便是最污穢的房間也能為之一新。
For sweetness of the body I have scented oils that will moisten the skin and inflame passions.	若要滋養肌膚，我這裡備有香油，能潤澤肌膚，撩動情慾。
My vases and bottles are made by the finest artisans. Feast your eyes upon the delicate colors.	我的花瓶與瓶罐皆出自名匠之手，且盡情飽覽這些精緻的色澤。
If you desire to buy, I am ready to serve you.	你若有意購買，我隨時為你效勞。
Here are the herbs, habibi. A pleasure to do business with you.	藥草在此，朋友。與你交易，是我的榮幸。
Here is the charcoal. Return any time I may be of further service.	炭在此。若還有需要，歡迎隨時再來。
Good sir, I am speechless! Surely my cousin, Achmed, has sent this through you as an offering of peace between us.	好心的先生，我真是說不出話來！這想必是我表兄阿賀密德託你送來，作為我倆和解的表示。
Now I am ashamed that I behaved in such a petty way. Please, I beg you, take this broom and give it to Achmed and he will know that this is my apology.	如今我為自己那般小器的行徑感到羞愧。求你把這把掃帚帶給阿賀密德，他自會明白這是我的歉意。
I detect an unusual look of wisdom in this old woman's eyes.	你察覺這位老婦人的眼中，透著一股不尋常的智慧。
The small green apples in her basket are native to this region and rather tart, I believe.	她籃裡的小青蘋果是本地土產，想來滋味相當酸澀。
That would be most unwise.	那實在不是明智之舉。
I hope you find what you seek, but I have no further help to give you.	但願你能尋得所求之物，只是我已無力再助你了。
Seek Fatima now! You have no time to waste.	速去尋找法提瑪！你已沒有時間可以浪費。
Your greed has betrayed you. You chose to sell what you should have given freely. You are not worthy. Be gone from my sight.	你的貪婪出賣了你。本該無私贈與之物，你卻選擇了販售。你不配得此殊榮，速從我眼前退下。
Nothing more will I say or give until you have completed every task.	在你完成每一項考驗之前，我不會再多說一句、多給一物。
You have made your choice. Now you must live with it.	你已做出抉擇，如今便須承受這抉擇的後果。
King Arthur, I know your purpose here. It is given to me to know such things, for I am a seeress.	亞瑟王，我知曉你此行的目的。這等事物我自能洞悉，因我是位女先知。
Another came from your land and his name was Galahad. He spoke of you, for if he failed, he knew only you might follow and succeed.	曾有一人從你的國度而來，名叫葛拉漢。他提起過你，因為他深知，若自己失敗，唯有你能繼之而成。
But as a servant of the Goddess, I must know you are worthy. I bid you to buy an apple, for this fruit is sacred to Aphrodite.	但身為女神的僕人，我必須確認你當得起此殊榮。我命你買下一顆蘋果，因這果實是阿芙羅黛蒂的聖物。
Buying the apple is but the first test I shall place before you, if you are ready.	買下這顆蘋果，不過是我為你設下的第一道考驗，如果你已準備好的話。
You have the apple that ends hunger, slakes thirst, and eases weariness. May it comfort you in time of greatest need.	你已得到這顆能止饑、解渴、消除疲憊的蘋果。願它在你最需要之時，予你慰藉。
You have purchased the only apple I will sell you.	你已買下我唯一願意賣給你的蘋果。
One apple, and one only, I will sell you. Here are your choices.	我只會賣給你一顆蘋果，僅此一顆。以下是你的選擇。
If you give me 1 fals, I will give you an apple that is only an apple and nothing more. Eat, and it will taste good.	若你給我一枚銅幣，我會給你一顆平凡無奇的蘋果。吃下去，滋味不錯。
If you give me 1 dirham, I will give you an apple that will satisfy all your hunger, slake all your thirst and ease your weariness.	若你給我一枚銀幣，我會給你一顆能止盡你的饑餓、解盡你的乾渴、消除你疲憊的蘋果。
If you give me 1 dinar, I will give you an apple that is bitter to the tongue, yet you will know the taste of Truth.	若你給我一枚金幣，我會給你一顆入口苦澀，卻能讓你嚐到真理滋味的蘋果。
It is obvious what I have and do not have.	我有什麼、沒有什麼，一目瞭然。
Give me nothing and you gain nothing.	你若什麼都不給，便什麼也得不到。
You have already bought the only apple I will sell you.	你已買下我唯一願意賣給你的蘋果了。
If you wish to buy an apple, please say so.	你若想買蘋果，儘管開口。
Nay, I need it not.	不，我不需要它。
Such things are not sacred to the Goddess.	這類東西並非女神的聖物。
I am a lesser servant of the Goddess and do not know where it is to be found. Only Fatima can provide the guidance you need.	我不過是女神座下的一名小小僕人，不知此物何處可尋。唯有法提瑪能給你所需的指引。
She is the great mother of all, whom we call Aphrodite	她是萬物的偉大母親，我們稱她為阿芙羅黛蒂
She is the Great Goddess, mother of the universe, creator of gods.	她是偉大的女神，宇宙之母，眾神的創造者。
I serve Aphrodite.	我侍奉阿芙羅黛蒂。
You have seen her. What more is there to say?	你已見過她了，還有什麼好說的？
You will learn about Fatima if you are found worthy.	若你被判定為當得起此殊榮，自會知曉法提瑪之事。
You will find her with the symbols of the Goddess, the star and crescent.	你能在女神的標識——星與新月——之處尋得她。
He came here only recently, after long weeks of search in other places. But I have not seen him for many days.	他是近日才到此地，之前在別處尋訪了數週之久。但我已有多日未曾見過他了。
I know nothing of them.	我對他們一無所知。
You must be a wise man to find a wise man.	唯有智者，方能尋得智者。
Whosoever you speak with in this bazaar will be compelled to speak the truth about what he or she most deeply needs or wants.	在這市集中，凡與你交談之人，皆會不由自主地道出內心最深切的渴求。
Your task is to do as your soul and heart dictate. Only you can decide what that means.	你的職責，是依循自己的靈魂與內心行事。這意味著什麼，唯有你自己能夠決定。
Speak with him and judge his character for yourself.	與他交談，親自評斷他的品格。
Only by seeking it will you be able to attain it.	唯有透過尋求，你才能有所得。
There are six Guardians whose tests you must pass. I am one of them.	共有六位守護者，你必須通過她們的考驗，而我便是其中之一。
It was not planned as a part of your test, if that is what you wonder.	你若在納悶，那並非我考驗你的一環。
A seeress knows which questions are worth answering and which should be ignored.	女先知自知哪些提問值得回答，哪些該置之不理。
Take this, and by my command, eat of it.	拿去，並依我之命，吃下它。
You have chosen wisely, for the apple has conferred upon you a Truth Spell. Whoever you speak with in this bazaar from this moment on will confide to you his or her most secret and urgent need.	你選得明智，這顆蘋果已賦予你真言術。從此刻起，在這市集中與你交談之人，皆會向你吐露內心最隱密、最迫切的需求。
To prove your full worthiness to me, and thus be led ever closer to your goal, you must fulfill these tasks revealed for you by the Truth Spell. Your heart and mind must guide you.	為了向我證明你完全當得起此殊榮，並藉此更接近你的目標，你必須完成真言術為你揭示的這些任務。你的心與意志必須引領著你。
You have eaten, but gained nothing. You failed my test and you will never possess the Grail. Your hopes die here.	你已吃下蘋果，卻一無所獲。你未能通過我的考驗，永遠也不會擁有聖杯。你的希望，就此終結。
She spoke true. The apple has eased all your hunger and thirst. New strength flows into your limbs.	她所言不虛。這顆蘋果已消除了你所有的饑渴，一股新的力量注入你的四肢。
You feel refreshed, yet you have failed miserably to pass my test. Your quest ends here. The Grail is denied to you.	你感到神清氣爽，然而你卻慘遭我的考驗所淘汰。你的探尋就此終止，聖杯與你無緣。
I greet you with reverence, King Arthur, for you are indeed worthy. Knowledge is your reward.	我以敬意迎接你，亞瑟王，因你確實當得起此殊榮。知識，便是你的獎賞。
Seek the star and crescent where Fatima dwells. Now that you are ready, she will admit you. She is the most powerful, though not the last, of the Guardians of the Sacred Cup.	尋著星與新月，前往法提瑪所居之處。如今你已準備就緒，她將接見你。她是聖杯守護者之中最有力者，卻並非最後一位。
So you have suffered a misfortune? Very well, I will help you again.	你竟遭逢此等不幸？也罷，我再助你一次。
Take also this gift.	再收下這件禮物吧。
It is the apple that ends hunger, slakes thirst, and eases weariness. May it comfort you in time of greatest need. The Goddess be with you.	這是能止饑、解渴、消除疲憊的蘋果。願它在你最需要之時，予你慰藉。願女神與你同在。
Here is an apple that will relieve all hunger and thirst and renew your strength.	這顆蘋果能消解一切饑渴，重振你的氣力。
Do not lose THIS one.	這一顆，你千萬別再弄丟了。
Let us say simply that it is someone's crude idea of a joke.	就這麼說吧，這不過是某人拙劣的惡作劇。
It is only graffiti.	這不過是塗鴉。
It is completely dark and deserted.	這裡一片漆黑，杳無人跡。
The walls are far too high to jump over.	這牆太高了，跳不過去。
The alley is paved with stone, solidly set. The thief could not have escaped through the ground.	這條巷子鋪著石板，結結實實。竊賊不可能從地面脫逃。
The bars are made of heavy iron.	這些欄杆是以厚重的鐵條打造。
It is a dead end alley with no doors and only two windows, one of which is bricked up and the other blocked by a heavy iron bar.	這是條死巷，沒有門，只有兩扇窗——一扇已被磚封死，另一扇則被厚重的鐵條擋住。
The thief quickly pulls up his rope so you cannot follow!	竊賊迅速將繩子收起，教你無法跟上！
The thief has escaped.	竊賊已然逃脫。
There is no sign of him at all.	完全不見他的蹤影。
The thief must have left behind a rope and climbed up it to escape.	竊賊想必是留下一條繩子，攀繩而上脫逃了。
The lower window is bricked up. Only a skinny man could squeeze into the upper window, if he had the means to reach it.	下方的窗戶已被磚封死。唯有瘦小之人，若有辦法搆得到，方能擠進上方的窗戶。
The walls are old and deteriorating on the surface, but solid underneath. No doors, no sign of hidden openings, no way to scale or climb them.	這些牆面古舊，表層已剝落，內裡卻依然堅實。沒有門，也不見任何暗藏的開口，無法攀爬翻越。
They are very old, but quite solid.	它們雖已老舊，卻十分堅固。
Judging from the smell, it is not something you want to step in.	從氣味判斷，那不是你會想踩上去的東西。
A dog carcass is busily rotting.	一具狗屍正腐爛著。
They swarm over the remains of the dog.	牠們群聚在狗的殘骸上。
I would prefer not to guess as to what that is.	那究竟是什麼，我寧可不去猜測。
The outer surface is crumbling. As for using the lower window as a foothold, you would not get far enough to do any good.	外層表面正在剝落。至於想拿下方的窗戶當立足點，你也搆不到什麼有用的地方。
Powerful though Excaliber is, it still has its limits. These bars would destroy the blade.	聖劍雖然威力強大，仍有其極限。這些鐵條會毀了劍身。
Had you followed him immediately, you might have at least had a chance to catch him. Now he could be anywhere.	你若立刻追上前去，至少還有機會逮住他。如今他已不知去向何方。
This thief was cunning enough to climb down a rope from the barred window, leave the rope hanging, then scurry back up the rope and escape.	這竊賊夠狡猾，先順著繩子從有欄杆的窗戶爬下，留下繩子懸著，再匆匆攀繩而上逃走。
Even Excaliber could not stop this quick and elusive thief.	即便是聖劍，也攔不住這身手敏捷、飄忽不定的竊賊。
The thief has escaped. And you would blunt your fine blade by hacking uselessly at these heavy iron bars.	竊賊已然逃脫。而你若徒勞劈砍這些厚重的鐵條，只會鈍了你那把好劍。
The combination of rotting dog and human excreta leaves much to be desired. Such as getting as far away from it as you can.	腐爛的狗屍混著人類排泄物，實在令人不敢恭維——比如，儘可能離它遠一點。
The dog is dead, putrid and full of disease, Arthur. Leave it be.	這狗已死，腐臭不堪，滿身病菌，亞瑟，別去碰它。
They are busy with the rotting dog.	牠們正忙著啃食那具腐爛的狗屍。
The thief is too quick for you.	竊賊的身手比你快得多。
The thief is gone.	竊賊已經走了。
The thief is too busy escaping.	竊賊正忙著逃命。
"Caupona" is the Latin for "inn" or "tavern". If I interpret the symbol below correctly, this is the "Star of Allah Inn".	「Caupona」在拉丁文中意為「客棧」或「酒館」。如果我沒解讀錯下方的符號，這裡便是「真主之星客棧」。
The grain merchant's agitation is so great, he will not stand still long enough to speak or do business.	這穀物商人心浮氣躁，連好好站著說話做生意的耐性都沒有。
Across the street are two merchants.	街道對面有兩名商人。
Next to the grain merchant's shop, there is an inn.	穀物商人的店鋪旁，有一間客棧。
It is a rather rundown place.	那是個相當破敗的地方。
You cannot see inside with Achmed blocking the door.	阿賀密德擋在門口，你看不見裡頭的情形。
Dare I say it? The inside does not look like an improvement on the outside. Still, he is offering his hospitality.	這話我也不知該不該說：裡頭似乎並不比外頭好上多少。不過，他仍盛情款待。
My Arabic is not quite good enough to translate that.	我的阿拉伯語還沒好到能翻譯這個。
The door is shut, to state the obvious.	這扇門是關著的，這是明擺著的事。
The door is partway open.	這扇門半掩著。
The door is open. You should either enter or move on.	這扇門開著。你該不進去，就得繼續前行。
Nothing can be seen through these windows.	透過這些窗戶，什麼也看不見。
It is too dim inside to make out much more than some crude tables and chairs.	裡頭光線昏暗，只能勉強看出幾張粗陋的桌椅。
The shutters are closed.	百葉窗是關著的。
It is not so much an alley as a gap between the buildings that is walled off. You can glimpse more back streets of Jerusalem, but nothing that is of use to you.	與其說是條巷子，不如說是建築之間被牆封住的一道縫隙。你能瞥見耶路撒冷更多的後街，但沒什麼對你有用的東西。
There is no one here to ask.	這裡沒有人可問。
The birds peck at grain spilt over from the merchant's pots.	鳥兒啄食著從商人罐子裡灑出的穀粒。
You startled the birds into flight.	你驚起了那群鳥，牠們飛走了。
The birds perch on the ledge, waiting for you to leave.	鳥兒棲在窗臺上，等著你離開。
He stands on the other side of his shop.	他站在自己店鋪的另一側。
Are you confused? There is no one here.	你糊塗了嗎？這裡沒有人。
It does not smell particularly inviting inside.	裡頭的氣味可稱不上誘人。
Achmed looks as rundown as his inn.	阿賀密德看起來和他的客棧一樣破敗。
I do not see him.	我沒看見他。
Achmed would let you in if he so desired.	阿賀密德若有意，自會讓你進去。
Well? Will you enter or not?	怎麼樣？你到底進不進去？
These windows cannot be opened from the outside.	這些窗戶無法從外面打開。
The door is already open.	這扇門已經開著了。
Talking to the door will not help.	對著門說話也無濟於事。
Believe me, I regret I cannot serve you. If only I had a broom.	相信我，我很遺憾無法招待你。要是我有把掃帚就好了。
Please enter, habibi. Allow me to show my gratitude by giving you food and drink while I clean up.	請進，朋友。且讓我以食物和飲水略表謝意，我這就去打掃。
Perhaps he cannot hear you call.	或許他聽不見你的呼喚。
Ah, I am in desperate need of a broom!	唉，我真是迫切需要一把掃帚！
Thank you so very much for the broom, habibi!	太感謝你送的這把掃帚了，朋友！
My cousin Tariq is angry with me and will not sell me a broom!	我表弟泰利克在生我的氣，不肯賣我掃帚！
I never believed my cousin would give me the broom. Allah be praised!	我從沒想過表弟會把掃帚送給我。讚美真主！
My inn is filthy. Only with a broom can I properly clean it.	我的客棧髒亂不堪，唯有一把掃帚才能將它徹底清理乾淨。
Come in! Come in! I am still cleaning, but you are welcome.	進來吧！進來吧！我還在打掃，但歡迎你進來。
</content>
</invoke>
